<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50680" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vescia</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little town in
				Latium</i>, <i>on the river Liris</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
			11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9,
			25</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vescīnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Vescia</i>, <i>Vescinian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 2, 25, 66</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 10, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 31</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 241</span></i>
			 (al. Vestinus).—In <i>neutr.
			subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Vescino,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 15, 2, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vescī-ni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Vescia</i>, <i>Vescinians</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				10, 20</span></i>.</div>
